.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH git-veil-verify-keyring 1  "git-veil-verify-keyring " 
.SH NAME
git\-veil\-verify\-keyring \- Verify the keyring signature against the pinned trusted key
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgit\-veil verify\-keyring\fR [\fB\-\-remote\fR] [\fB\-\-key\-store\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Verify the keyring signature against the pinned trusted key
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-remote\fR \fI<REMOTE>\fR [default: origin]
Git remote name
.TP
\fB\-\-key\-store\fR \fI<KEY_STORE>\fR
Key store directory (default: $GIT_VEIL_HOME or $HOME/.git\-veil)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.SH EXTRA
Verifies the keyring\*(Aqs signature against the pinned trusted key for this
repository. Fail\-closed: without an established trust pin (git\-veil
trust) on this machine, or when the signature does not verify, the
command exits with an error. Every gated command (hide, reveal, cat,
unhide, changes, tell, removeperson, list\-keys) runs this same check
before touching secrets.

EXAMPLES
  $ git\-veil verify\-keyring
  $ git\-veil verify\-keyring \-\-remote upstream
